<!--
Illustrative custom rule for repeated SSH invalid-user events.
This is a starting point, not a portable or production-ready detection.

Before use:
1. Inspect installed SSH rules and test an actual event with
   /var/ossec/bin/wazuh-logtest (or Dashboard > Tools > Ruleset test).
2. Confirm parent ID, decoded srcip field, time window, and frequency
   behavior in your release. This example assumes rule 5710 and srcip.
   Current docs use 5710 for an SSH invalid-user event; versions/log formats differ.
3. Wazuh custom-rule guidance recommends IDs 100000-120000. Check local
   collisions before selecting 100100.
4. Back up local_rules.xml. Place custom rules in /var/ossec/etc/rules/,
   not /var/ossec/ruleset/rules/ (managed by Wazuh and may change on upgrade).
5. Validate positive and negative cases. This does not detect all failed SSH
   passwords or Windows logon failures.

No active response is configured by this example.
-->
<group name="local,authentication,">
  <rule id="100100" level="10" frequency="5" timeframe="120">
    <if_matched_sid>5710</if_matched_sid>
    <same_srcip />
    <description>Repeated SSH invalid-user events from the same source IP (lab example)</description>
    <mitre>
      <id>T1110</id>
    </mitre>
    <group>authentication_failed,ssh,</group>
  </rule>
</group>
